From 67a56d087176e493851278ab969f7514ee7d972a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 21:09:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] fix: none of the product's transitions were actually
 running

Measuring the shell in a real browser turned up that a nav link's computed
transitionDuration was 0s. It should have been 160ms.

duration-[--motion-fast] was valid in Tailwind v3, which wrapped a bare
custom property in var() for you. v4 does not. The compiled rule was
transition-duration: --motion-fast -- an invalid value the browser drops.
Eighteen usages across twelve files, dating to phase 1.5: every hover,
focus and colour transition in the portal, the admin and the forms, plus
the active-item rule in the nav. The interface never looked broken, only
dry, which is why it survived three phases of review.

rounded-[--radius] was worse: it pointed at a token that does not exist,
since the tokens are --radius-sm/md/lg.

All of it moves to v4's parenthesis form. Chromium confirms the fix:
0s becomes 0.16s, and reduced motion still wins at 1e-05s.

Two rules kept surviving a clean rebuild, which nearly hid the whole thing
from the audit -- Tailwind v4 scans the entire project, and patches/*.patch
carries the diff of every phase, so classes fixed in code came back through
their own history as dead CSS. @source not excludes them.

A source guard now fails on -[--token] anywhere in src, with a companion
case asserting the correct form is in use so the guard cannot pass by
matching nothing.

